8,369,16774,4767,11,8110,553,279,4236,11178,369,19067,323,13391,448,279,2326,11178,369,95391,13,758,1246,1657,5510,646,279,11178,387,10007,389,279,25853,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nOn the student government ballot at Dusable High School, the six candidates for president are listed first, followed by the four candidates for vice president, followed by the five candidates for secretary and ending with the three candidates for treasurer. In how many ways can the candidates be listed on the ballot?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"8a3c73df1c5f505e907ddd874ef0f599eb05853afdb5b6e04a378753b10d176c"},"seconds":27.0109646320343,"seed":1088861322270219861,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem of determining the number of ways the candidates can be listed on the ballot, we need to consider the separate groupings of candidates for each position and then combine these groups.\n\nFirst, let's consider the number of ways to arrange the candidates within each position:\n- There are 6 candidates for president, and they can be arranged in \\(6!\\) (6 factorial) ways.\n- There are 4 candidates for vice president, and they can be arranged in \\(4!\\) (4 factorial) ways.\n- There are 5 candidates for secretary, and they can be arranged in \\(5!\\) (5 factorial) ways.\n- There are 3 candidates for treasurer, and they can be arranged in \\(3!\\) (3 factorial) ways.\n\nCalculating each factorial:\n- \\(6! = 720\\)\n- \\(4! = 24\\)\n- \\(5! = 120\\)\n- \\(3! = 6\\)\n\nNext, since the candidates for each position are grouped together in a specific order (president, then vice president, then secretary, then treasurer), we do not need to consider the arrangement of these groups relative to each other. We simply multiply the number of ways to arrange the candidates within each group.\n\nThus, the total number of ways to list all the candidates on the ballot is:\n\\[\n6! \\times 4! \\times 5! \\times 3!\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the factorial values:\n\\[\n720 \\times 24 \\times 120 \\times 6\n\\]\n\nCalculating step by step:\n\\[\n720 \\times 24 = 17280\n\\]\n\\[\n17280 \\times 120 = 2073600\n\\]\n\\[\n2073600 \\times 6 = 12441600\n\\]\n\nThus, the total number of ways to list the candidates on the ballot is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{12441600}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{12441600}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
